===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q677}}{{lb|en|uncountable}} A common, inexpensive metal, silvery grey when untarnished, that rusts, is attracted by magnets, and is used in making [[steel]]: a chemical [[element]] having [[atomic number]] 26 and symbol {{l|mul|Fe}}.
#: {{syn|en|ferrum}}
#: {{hyper|en|metal#Noun|<|element#Noun|;|substance#Noun|;|material#Noun}}
#* {{seeCites|en}}
# {{senseid|en|any nonsteel material mostly made of Fe}} {{lb|en|uncountable|countable|metallurgy}} Any material, not a [[steel]], predominantly made of elemental iron.
#: {{hyper|en|metal#Noun|<|substance#Noun|;|material#Noun}}
#: {{hypo|en|cast iron#Noun|ductile iron#Noun|gray iron#Noun|pig iron#Noun|white iron#Noun|wrought iron#Noun}}
# {{senseid|en|Q483634}}{{lb|en|countable}} A [[tool]] or [[appliance]] made of [[metal]], which is [[heat]]ed and then used to [[transfer]] heat to something else; most often a [[thick]] [[piece]] of metal fitted with a [[handle]] and having a [[flat]], roughly [[triangular]] [[bottom]], which is heated and used to [[press]] [[wrinkle]]s from [[clothing]], and now usually containing an [[electrical]] heating [[apparatus]].
#: {{syn|en|clothes iron|flatiron|smoothing iron}}
#: {{hypo|en|box iron|charcoal iron|steam iron}}
#: {{cot|en|clothes press|mangle}}
# {{senseid|en|any of various tools made mostly of Fe}} Any of several other [[tool#Noun|tool]]s traditionally made of [[wrought iron]], now usually of [[steel]].
#: {{hyper|en|tool#Noun}}
#: {{hypo|en|pinking iron#Noun|plane iron#Noun|plough iron#Noun|ripping iron#Noun|tamping iron#Noun|tire iron#Noun}}
# {{lb|en|usually|in the plural|'''''[[irons]]'''''}} [[shackle|Shackles]].
#: {{hypo|en|leg irons}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[firearm]], either a [[long gun]] or a [[handgun]].
#: {{syn|en|shooting iron}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=1948|writer=w:John Huston|title={{w|The Treasure of the Sierra Madre (film)|Treasure of the Sierra Madre}}|passage=Ah, throw that old '''iron''' over here! We'll pick it up and go on our way.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1959|author=w:Marty Robbins|title=w:Big Iron|passage=the stranger there among them had a big '''iron''' on his hip}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A dark shade of the [[color]] [[silver]].
# {{lb|en|countable|Cockney rhyming slang|offensive|shortened from '''[[iron hoof]]'''|rhyming with '''[[poof]]'''}} A male [[homosexual]].
#: {{syn|en|poof|queer|Thesaurus:male homosexual}}
# {{lb|en|golf}} A [[golf club]] used for middle-distance shots.
#: {{hypo|en|driving iron|long iron|short iron|1-iron|2-iron|3-iron|4-iron|5-iron|6-iron|7-iron|8-iron|9-iron}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1902|author=Robert Marshall Grade|title=The Haunted Major
|passage=The brassey much resembled the driver, but the '''iron''' opened out quite a new field of practice; {{...}}}}
# {{senseid|en|tough}} {{lb|en|uncountable|figurative}} {{n-g|Used as a symbol of great strength or toughness, or to signify a very strong or tough material.}}
#: {{ux|en|[[ironman|'''iron'''man]]; a will of '''iron'''}}
#: {{ux|en|He appeared easygoing, but inside he was pure '''iron'''.}}
# {{lb|en|weightlifting}} [[weight|Weight]] used as [[resistance]] for the purpose of [[strength training]].
#: {{ux|en|He lifts '''iron''' on the weekends.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|astronomy|geology}} A [[meteorite]] consisting primarily of metallic iron (mixed with a small amount of [[nickel]]), as opposed to one composed mainly of [[stony]] material.
#: {{ux|en|'''Irons''' and stony '''irons''' can be much larger than stony meteorites and are much more visually striking, but make up only a few percent of all meteorites.}}
# A [[safety curtain]] in a theatre.
# {{lb|en|military|slang}} {{cap|dumb bomb}}s, those without [[guidance]] [[system]]s.

